  "changelog": "Arbor 1.0 replaces the tiered state machine. The main agent writes the contract, splits the work into node files under the task's `nodes/` directory and reacts to `arbor.py sync`; every node is one Orca worker in its own worktree, merged into the task's integration branch when its commits stay inside its paths; the gate on the merged result is the judge. Installed for Claude Code: the `CLAUDE.md` block and the skill `arbor` (loaded on demand) plus the kept skills `arbor-update-spec` and `arbor-spec-bootstrap`; for Codex: the `AGENTS.md` block and the kept skills. Removed: all four hooks (`.claude/hooks/*`, `.codex/hooks/*`, `.codex/hooks.json`, the hook entries of `.claude/settings.json`), the six role files `.arbor/agents/*.md`, `.arbor/workflow.md`, the slash commands and skills `start`, `continue`, `finish-work`, `workflow`, `before-dev`, `check`, `break-loop`, `brainstorm` and `arbor-meta`, and the driver scripts `task.py`, `get_context.py`, `check_report.py` with their modules. `.arbor/config.yaml` is never rewritten by `arbor update` any more; `executors.<default>.agent` still works as the `write` agent; the optional `executors.<default>.agents.<write|explore|review|light>` (an agent id, or `agent` with `model` and `effort`) and `executors.<default>.max_nodes` keys are new.",
