  "configSectionsAdded": [],
  "migrationGuide": "1. Before updating, finish or abandon every started task with the old version (`arbor.py finish` or `arbor.py abandon` of 0.11): 1.0 refuses a task.json written before 1.0 and cannot continue it.\n2. Run `arbor update --migrate`. It deletes the removed hooks, role files, workflow.md, commands, skills and driver scripts; files you never edited go without asking, edited ones are asked about (`--migrate -f` deletes them after a backup, `--migrate -s` keeps them). In a `.claude/settings.json` you edited, only the entries that run a deleted Arbor hook are removed; your own hooks and settings stay. An unedited `.codex/hooks.json` is deleted, an edited one keeps your own entries.\n3. Codex's \"Hooks need review\" prompt no longer applies: Arbor installs no hooks.\n4. Orca creates worktrees only for its projects. Arbor adds the repositories a task touches (the control repository and the `git: true` package repositories) itself with `orca repo add` when the task starts; nothing to do by hand.\n5. Optional: pick the agent of each kind of work under `executors.<default>.agents` in `.arbor/config.yaml`: `write` (nodes with paths; your old `agent:` still works), `explore` (read-only nodes), `review` (reviewer nodes), `light` (mechanical edits). An entry is an agent id, or `agent` with `model` and `effort`. Also `max_nodes` bounds the nodes of one task (default 30). The commented example in a fresh `arbor init` shows the shape."
}
